+Searched the repository, Downloads, potential uploads/attachment locations, temporary attachment directories, `C:\Temp` and `C:\app`. Existing unrelated exercise datasets were not substituted for these recordings.
+
+## Manifest to complete
+
+`labels.local.json` contains exactly the requested fields: `file`, `exercise_guess`, `camera_facing`, `plate_occluded`, `full_reps`, `partial_reps`, `notes`. File paths are verified facts; guesses are filename text with attempt suffixes removed. Everything else is null.
+
+For each clip:
+
+- Confirm/correct `exercise_guess`, including whether narrow-grip rows are alternating. Keep seated dips, triceps pushdown and weighted dips distinct.
+- Fill `camera_facing` with front/back, or leave null if unknown.
+- Fill `plate_occluded` with true/false after review, or leave null if unknown. Add occlusion times and affected joints in notes where relevant.
+- Fill `full_reps` and `partial_reps` with reviewed integer counts. Zero means an observed zero; null means unknown. Include the counting unit (per arm, bilateral cycle, alternating pair) and set boundaries in notes.
+- Use `notes` for uncertainty and time-specific form-cue adjudication. Counts alone cannot establish whether a cue was false. To score false cues later, provide rule/time intervals where an independent reviewer says the fault is present, absent or unassessable.
+
+A labeled subset is sufficient to begin a baseline. If labels cannot be established from a recording, keep the corresponding metric unmeasured.
+
+## Replay routes tried, in order
+
+1. Headless Chromium via installed Edge, explicitly with `--no-sandbox`, `--disable-setuid-sandbox`, `--use-gl=angle`, `--use-angle=swiftshader`, `--enable-unsafe-swiftshader` and `--disable-dev-shm-usage`. Launch failed with `browserType.launch: Target page, context or browser has been closed` and `TransactNamedPipe: The pipe has been ended. (0x6D)`. The full stack, launch flags and browser log are retained in `replay-environment-log.json`.
+2. Python imports: MediaPipe **0.10.14** and OpenCV **4.11.0** succeeded. Importing the optional `imageio_ffmpeg` wrapper failed with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pkg_resources'`. No dependencies were installed. Located its already-installed `ffmpeg-win64-v4.2.2.exe` and invoked that executable directly.
+3. That ffmpeg binary decoded three actual RGB frames; MediaPipe Tasks VIDEO/CPU ran the local model; the Node bridge processed the real landmark outputs with the current app counter. The command completed successfully. Infrastructure result: **3 frames, 0 frames missing both configured working triplets**. Python CPU inference p95 over ONLY those three initial frames was **84.9444 ms**. This small startup sample is not an exercise-set or steady-state performance baseline and is not evidence that any acceptance threshold passed.
+
+Model SHA-256: `59929e1d1ee95287735ddd833b19cf4ac46d29bc7afddbbf6753c459690d574a`.
+
+Video SHA-256: `dcf3765b43bcc9a84f71ba57104c3ac38048add2fd6117b6b76c213f2e0c722d`.
+
+The runtime backend differs from browser WASM/native phone inference. Identical model bytes and counter source do not establish cross-backend detector parity. The bridge only injects read-only state diagnostics in memory; app source files are unchanged. Python replay does not run the physical camera, native startup gate, spoken-cue controller, React lifecycle, thermal handling or live scheduler.
+
+## Baseline status
+
+| Metric on a labeled full set | Current result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Full-rep count error per exercise | Unmeasured — no reviewed counts |
+| Partial-rep count error per exercise | Unmeasured — no reviewed counts |
+| Frames with missing working joints over each clip | Unmeasured — only a three-frame infrastructure probe ran |
+| False form cue rate, including plate-occluded footage | Unmeasured — no independent cue/time annotations |
+| Per-exercise p95 inference latency | Unmeasured — no complete labeled set replay |
+| Device temperature/thermal state, memory trend, live drops, camera restarts | Unmeasured — no device soak |
+
+Predicted counts from the three-frame probe are not a set count, ground truth, or an error measurement. No before/after behavioral comparison exists. Stop for annotated current-code baseline review before implementing fixes.
+
+## Patch series and soak additions
+
+All deliverable changes are patches under `patches/`, with inspectable payload copies under `patches/files/`. No `.git` workaround or index write was attempted. `git apply --check` is a read-only worktree check, not staging.
+
+- `0001-local-video-labels-and-inventory.patch`: requested simple manifest and exact path/size/hash inventory.
+- `0002-browser-free-replay.patch`: ffmpeg/Python/Node replay tool and usage notes; no runtime app changes.
+- `0003-soak-plan-thermal-latency-endpoints.patch`: thermal state or actual sensor temperature when available; one-minute p50/p90/p95/p99/max latency trends; pull-up/dip endpoint evidence checks.
+- `0004-local-resume-evidence.patch`: this stop report and exact environment error/smoke evidence.
+
+For a pull-up, full arm extension is at the bottom; for a dip, it is at the top. The plan requires BOTH exercise-specific endpoints in the same visible bounded cycle before an event can be judged full, rather than incorrectly requiring straight elbows at the bottom of a dip. No endpoint rule has been changed in the counter in this pass.
+
+Apply from the repository root on the intended worktree:
+
+```powershell
+git apply --check patches/0001-local-video-labels-and-inventory.patch patches/0002-browser-free-replay.patch patches/0003-soak-plan-thermal-latency-endpoints.patch patches/0004-local-resume-evidence.patch
+git apply patches/0001-local-video-labels-and-inventory.patch patches/0002-browser-free-replay.patch patches/0003-soak-plan-thermal-latency-endpoints.patch patches/0004-local-resume-evidence.patch
+```
+
+The patches add new files; they do not modify the current pose tracker. The editable `patches/labels.local.json` is the immediate labeling handoff. Applying patch 1 creates the initial null-filled template in `docs/pose-replay/labels.local.json`; it does not copy later edits from the handoff file. Point `--manifest` to whichever file you actually reviewed.
